WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:03.720
Ugh, the holidays!

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.100
On Thanksgiving, Americans gather to break
bread and share what they’re grateful for.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.850
But what should you do if you don’t feel
thankful?

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:14.980
Maybe your boss is a jerk.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.710
Maybe money is tight.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:20.840
Maybe you’re dreading awkward political
arguments with your relatives.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.160
Whatever the reason, you’re not feeling
the holiday spirit – so what are you supposed

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.160
to do?

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.599
Three words: Act grateful anyway.

00:00:28.599 --> 00:00:33.830
Social science shows that choosing to practice
gratitude, no matter how you feel, can itself

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.330
make you more grateful – and happier, too.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:40.479
One 2003 study found that people who kept
a list of things they were grateful for were

00:00:40.479 --> 00:00:44.450
significantly more satisfied with their lives
than subjects who dwelled on negative, or

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.300
even neutral, events instead.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.230
And thankfulness is contagious.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:52.470
A 2011 study found that responding to an angry
person with warmth and gratitude disarms their

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:54.650
aggression and leads to better behavior.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:01:00.040
So here’s the prescription for the holiday
blues: Forget about your feelings, and decide

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.050
to count your blessings.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.620
It’ll make you a happier person.

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:06.280
And it’ll probably make your dinner companions
happier, too.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.320
What do you think about the research on gratitude?

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.160
Let us know in your comments.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.530
Also, let us know what other topics you’d
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:20.619
and be sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

